  "exact_successor_authorization_text": "I approve one bounded direct MiniMax API Lumi 100-row response-only provider canary from this exact local workspace. Bind immutable source registry v0.17 SHA-256 85a688a62be0902b177469c99eb31525fb633efab5e420416b705d03e8d80e1a, closure plan v0.4 SHA-256 0a722beab289cbd391348406e2f1ac37f403daaaee1f4657f66a5f613bba06a0, closure report SHA-256 d8ad6eeda1f2c267809cd6ea1102d81541e6b850f87ffc5792e3b5fe8c31c29f, closure verification SHA-256 78555258ff06b79f146419cfb039d73067098a3031e74d8f9af4abe158637419, frozen tokenizer.json SHA-256 1022c9538d9ec795b07c2e2bda3c5c6f21c321de933cfe5ad197628a94caa2ee, chat template SHA-256 bc7853a9277feddae2fd3db786c6a12f4fa3602a135a0408c38d4390f33bec12, and benchmark-signature registry v0.3 SHA-256 1ffb5e938ab28c2fc876b9efd6c6ed59059f1e85aed2c396c024ae5925a4745e. Use only direct endpoint https://api.minimax.io/v1 with exact model ID MiniMax-M2.7 under the MiniMax Open Platform Terms effective March 30, 2026; I attest that my account, purchase, and service order add no restriction prohibiting use of generated content to train Lumi. Read MINIMAX_API_KEY only from the local process environment without printing, storing, hashing, or transmitting the key anywhere except the provider Authorization header. Do not use Ollama Cloud because its May 2026 terms prohibit developing competing products; do not install or run Qwen, GPT-OSS, or any local model. Generate exactly the fresh deterministic 100-record schedule SHA-256 e5d2f4f648b42cbaf80b4ae65242390f7481a8ec0377359288767714b0cc0579, containing exactly four train rows and one validation row from each frozen five-task by four-language cell, under prompt contract lumi.minimax-teacher.response-only-provider-canary.v0.1. The provider may generate only assistant_response; the runner must attach frozen user_prompt, scenario_id, safety_label, tool_call, tool_result, split, task, language, and truthful AI-assisted provenance deterministically, while tool results remain deterministic and are never model-generated. Send only synthetic, rights-clear prompts with no secrets, PII, user data, production data, candidate text, or reasoning text. Use at most 2 attempts per record, a 2,048 generated-token ceiling per call, 120 sequential inference calls, 20 retry calls, 100 accepted outputs, 52,428,800 network bytes, 67,108,864 private write bytes, 90 runtime-minutes, and $1.00 total provider spend before tax at the observed standard price of $0.30 per million input tokens and $1.20 per million output tokens. Require at least 85 accepted rows, at least 85% overall acceptance, at least four of five accepted rows in every task-language cell, zero critical factual, safety, or tool failures, 5,500 to 12,000 retained train supervised tokens, at most 3,000 retained validation supervised tokens, and a deterministic 20-row owner-review packet with exactly one accepted row per cell and at least 90% owner acceptance. Apply the frozen schema, rights, provenance, secret, PII, benchmark-decontamination, tokenizer, chat-template, assistant-and-tool-only masking, 4K-fit, language, punctuation, factual-grounding, safety, timed-plan arithmetic, tool-result-verification, exact-duplicate, split-overlap, and MinHash 0.9 gates. Retain only accepted final candidate text; retain rejected attempts only as validation error, non-sensitive finish_reason, usage token counts, cost, latency, and request/response-envelope hashes without raw candidate or reasoning text. Stop early when any threshold becomes mathematically impossible or any call, retry, spend, runtime, network, or write cap is reached; write one aggregate cell-level failure report and do not enter a one-row repair loop. This canary cannot authorize 3.2M-token generation. No Ollama Cloud, server tools, web search, model download, package installation, registry change, dataset seal, active data-contract change, SFT training, production promotion, S3 action, remote host access, new instance, instance action, external distribution, unrelated access, or human-authorship claim.",
